        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Interleave separate position, color, and UV arrays into vertex format.</para>
<para>nvblox stores mesh vertex positions and colors in separate arrays (struct-of-arrays), but Vulkan expects a single interleaved vertex buffer (array-of-structs). This kernel converts between the two layouts on the GPU, writing directly into the CUDA/Vulkan shared buffer so no additional copy is required before rendering.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>positions</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CUDA device pointer to float positions (x, y, z per vertex). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>colors</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CUDA device pointer to uint8 colors (r, g, b per vertex). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>uvs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CUDA device pointer to float UVs (u, v per vertex), or nullptr if no UVs (all UVs set to -1,-1). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>output</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CUDA device pointer to output <ref refid="structnvblox_1_1renderer_1_1MeshVertex" kindref="compound">MeshVertex</ref> array. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>num_vertices</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of vertices. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>stream</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CUDA stream. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
